  "intro": "Fourth graders read longer words by using letter-sound patterns, syllables, and word parts (prefixes, suffixes, and roots). Breaking a long word into syllables or parts makes it readable. For example, 'unhappiness' = un + happi + ness, meaning the state of not being happy.",
